---
// Part 3 — copy from "Copy update 28 Sept" (docs/). Three choices, one per level
// of the movement; hovering one widens it and brings up its photograph. Each
// opens its section below: a 70ch column broken up by full-bleed <Scene>s. The
// photographs are from Unsplash (credits in src/assets/story/README.md); the
// You section's copy is from the AgreeOnTea campaign doc (docs/).
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Scene from '../components/Scene.astro';
import ReadProgress from '../components/ReadProgress.astro';
import tea from '../assets/story/you-01-tea-mugs.jpg';
import spread from '../assets/story/you-02-spread-the-word.jpg';
import plan from '../assets/story/you-03-the-plan.jpg';
import community from '../assets/story/community-06-we-the-people-of.jpg';
import chamber from '../assets/story/country-01-chamber.jpg';
import stage from '../assets/story/country-02-the-mall.jpg';
import following from '../assets/story/country-03-following.jpg';
import festival from '../assets/story/country-04-festival.jpg';
import child from '../assets/story/country-05-child.jpg';
import celebration from '../assets/story/country-06-jubilee.jpg';
// the level panels' photos: royalty-free from Unsplash
import communityPanel from '../assets/story/level-community.jpg';
import countryPanel from '../assets/story/level-country.jpg';

const LEVELS = [
  {
    id: 'you',
    n: 'I',
    lines: ['You'],
    teaser: 'Start with a 10-minute cup of tea.',
    image: tea,
  },
  {
    id: 'community',
    n: 'II',
    lines: ['Your', 'Community'],
    teaser: 'Hold a Council of the People where you live.',
    image: communityPanel,
    focus: '50% 25%',
  },
  {
    id: 'country',
    n: 'III',
    lines: ['Our', 'Country'],
    teaser: 'A National Council of the People on Immigration.',
    image: countryPanel,
    focus: '50% 40%',
  },
];

---

<Layout title="Be Part of It — We The People" introLines={['Be Part', 'of It']}>
  <PageHero lines={['Be Part', 'of It']}>
    <p class="hero__kicker fade-up">Part 03</p>
  </PageHero>

  <ReadProgress />
  <main>
    <p class="levels__intro">
      Here are ways to help make it happen by yourself, in your community and for our
      country.
    </p>

    <nav class="levels" aria-label="Ways to be part of it">
      {
        LEVELS.map((l) => (
          <a class="level" href={`#${l.id}`} data-level={l.id}>
            <Image
              class="level__img"
              src={l.image}
              alt=""
              style={l.focus && `object-position:${l.focus}`}
              widths={[480, 960]}
              sizes="(max-width: 720px) 100vw, 50vw"
              format="webp"
              quality={70}
            />
            <span class="level__n">{l.n}</span>
            <span class="level__title">
              {l.lines.map((line, i) => (
                <>
                  {i > 0 && <br />}
                  {line}
                </>
              ))}
            </span>
            <span class="level__teaser">{l.teaser}</span>
            <span class="level__cta" aria-hidden="true">
              ↓
            </span>
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </nav>

    <!-- I: YOU ------------------------------------------------------------- -->
    <article class="prose level-section" id="you">
      <Scene first src={tea} alt="Two pairs of hands around mugs of milky tea on a wooden table" kicker="I · You" heading="Can you #AgreeOnTea?" />

      <p class="lead">
        Even in these divided times, there is surely one last thing we Brits can agree on…
      </p>
      <p class="pull">Tea.</p>
      <p>
        Could you have a 10-minute cuppa with someone from a different political tribe to talk
        about a difficult topic?
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Perhaps with the family member that you've given up talking politics with.</li>
        <li>Your next-door neighbour who votes for that political party.</li>
        <li>Your workmate who doesn't see the world your way at all.</li>
        <li>
          Or even that person you avoid in the street because they look like they belong to
          the other side.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you do, then in the time it takes your tea to cool down, maybe you'll cool down the
        country a little too.
      </p>
      <p>
        When We The People choose to talk and listen to each other with respect, we challenge
        the perception of our insurmountable division.
      </p>
      <p>
        And we might discover there's more humanity and nuance among us than the algorithm or
        our politicians and media want us to believe.
      </p>
      <p>And that means we can come back together to find a way through our problems after all.</p>

      <h2>The Idea</h2>
      <p>The idea is to hold a respectful, honest conversation across our tribal lines.</p>
      <p>Where both sides are free to speak and be heard; where any perspective can be expressed.</p>
      <p>Of course, it's going to take courage. It's going to take backbone.</p>
      <p>Even more so, because the topic for this tea is one of the most difficult we face:</p>
      <p class="pull">What do you think about immigration and how this country might approach it?</p>

      <Scene src={plan} alt="A quiet lane running straight ahead through a tunnel of trees towards the light" heading="The Plan" focus="50% 60%" />
      <p>Here's how we suggest you go about it:</p>

      <section class="stage" aria-labelledby="stage-brew">
        <p class="stage__when">The Beginning</p>
        <h3 id="stage-brew">Gentle Brew</h3>
        <p>
          This first step is the most important. While you wait for the tea to brew, and add
          milk and sugar, make sure you check in as human beings first. How are you, what's on
          your mind or going on in your life right now?
        </p>
        <p>
          Since so many of us have passionate views about immigration, it's good to connect as
          people before you dive in!
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- the middle is the game itself: the rules as a card you could hold -->
      <section class="game-card" aria-labelledby="stage-dialogue">
        <header class="game-card__head">
          <p class="stage__when">The Middle</p>
          <h3 id="stage-dialogue">Dialogue</h3>
          <p class="game-card__meta">
            <span>2 players</span><span>3 rounds or more</span><span>90 seconds each</span>
          </p>
        </header>
        <p>It's simple: each person has at least 3 rounds of 90 seconds each to speak.</p>
        <ol class="game-card__rules">
          <li>When one person speaks, the other must listen. No interruptions.</li>
          <li>
            When it's your turn to speak, you give your honest and heartfelt point of view. No
            sugar-coating.
          </li>
          <li>
            When it's your turn to listen, you really listen – rather than just thinking about
            what you're going to say next.
          </li>
          <li>
            It's best to use an alarm for timings so that you're free to engage with the other
            person, not your phone.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="game-card__golden">
          <strong>The golden rule:</strong> be sure to avoid insults. Treat the other person how
          you would like to be treated in turn.
        </p>
        <p class="game-card__go">And if you want to do more than 3 rounds, go for it!</p>
      </section>

      <section class="stage" aria-labelledby="stage-reflect">
        <p class="stage__when">The End</p>
        <h3 id="stage-reflect">A Minute to Reflect</h3>
        <p>Once you both feel done, take one last minute to reflect on the process with each other.</p>
        <p>
          Don't feel disheartened about how much you disagreed. It's unlikely a single tea would
          change anyone's minds!
        </p>
        <p>Rather consider if there was even a moment of empathy for the other's point of view?</p>
        <p>
          Did you find even a single square inch of shared ground or catch a glimpse, no matter
          how brief, of the human beyond the divide?
        </p>
        <p>If the journey to come back together is 10,000 miles, then that would be a first step.</p>
      </section>

      <Scene src={spread} alt="Two women talking close on a city street at night, lights blurred behind them" heading="Spread the Word" focus="50% 40%" />
      <p>
        The most important thing is that the conversation happens at all. So if you want to keep
        it entirely private, that's totally fine.
      </p>
      <p>
        Or just share a photo of your two hands, your cups or your mugs, tagging #AgreeOnTea and
        @WeThePeopleGather.
      </p>
      <p>
        Of course, you can go further and share audio or video of the whole or part of the
        conversation.
      </p>
      <p>
        If others hear that you two did #AgreeOnTea, it might inspire them to do the same –
        perhaps even create a wave of reconnection across the country.
      </p>
      <p>In this way, we can all do our bit to show a more united, hopeful future is possible.</p>
    </article>

    <!-- II: YOUR COMMUNITY ------------------------------------------------- -->
    <article class="prose level-section" id="community">
      <Scene first src={community} alt="A woman laughing with her hands over her mouth, talking with friends at a table" kicker="II · Your Community" heading="We The People of…" focus="50% 40%" />

      <p class="lead">Dover. Brixton. Edinburgh. Piddington. York. Cardiff. Hastings — and more.</p>
      <p>
        The issue of immigration has touched many of our communities, both for good and for
        ill.
      </p>
      <p>
        The divisions we see in the country find their way into our day-to-day lives and the
        places we call home. Even our family tables.
      </p>
      <!-- a solid green band, out to the viewport edges like a <Scene>, carrying
           the turn from the problem to the two paths below -->
      <p class="paths-banner">
        So we offer two paths to hold a Council of the People for your community, whatever
        its size.
      </p>

      <h2>Download our toolkit</h2>
      <p>
        Access our free toolkit (coming soon) for a clear step-by-step process, principles
        and resources to hold a gathering yourself.
      </p>
      <p>We can also connect you with a network of expert facilitators in your area, if required.</p>

      <h2>Let Us Help</h2>
      <p>
        Please <a href="mailto:hello@wethepeoplegather.com">get in touch</a> if you would
        like our direct support in holding a Council of the People in your community.
      </p>
      <p>
        We can provide bespoke guidance on setting up a Council and also offer impartial
        facilitation for the Council itself.
      </p>
      <p>
        If we do not have capacity for our team to attend on the day, we will endeavour to
        connect you with a facilitator team in your area that can do the same job.
      </p>
      <p>
        Though it is up to you to source an appropriate venue, provide refreshments and
        advertise, we offer our services at no cost.
      </p>

      <p class="pull">
        The dream: to inspire a wave of reconnection and reconciliation in communities
        across the country.
      </p>
    </article>

    <!-- III: OUR COUNTRY --------------------------------------------------- -->
    <article class="prose level-section" id="country">
      <Scene first src={chamber} alt="An empty horseshoe-shaped debating chamber, rows of seats facing the centre" kicker="III · Our Country" heading="A National Council of the People" />

      <p class="lead">
        Starting with you, through your community, we hope that the wave of reconnection and
        reconciliation will culminate in a major cultural event: a National Council of the
        People on Immigration.
      </p>
      <p>
        Using the Citizens' Assembly approach (see <a href="/hope">Our Real Hope</a>), we
        will select a group of 100 or more everyday people to discuss
      </p>
      <p class="pull">How might we approach immigration as a country?</p>
      <p>
        Lasting for up to two weeks, the Council will hear testimony from experts on
        immigration as well as personal stories of those whose lives have been affected by
        the issue.
      </p>
      <p>
        These could include positive stories of the beauty of British culture or
        contributions made by refugees. Or they could be negative stories of racist attacks
        or violence perpetrated by immigrants.
      </p>
      <p>
        It will be a place where all sides can speak without fear of judgment. Where ghosts
        from the past can be faced. Where we can express anger, grief, even shed tears.
      </p>
      <p>
        An opportunity for the communities of this island to share their stories at last, in
        search of a more united, hopeful future.
      </p>

      <Scene src={stage} alt="A man up on a friend's shoulders taking a photo, in a crowd on The Mall with a Union Jack behind" heading="A Moment of National Cultural Impact" focus="50% 25%" />
      <p>
        In that way, the national Council of the People aims to have a positive impact
        across our society.
      </p>
      <p>
        To that end, we will aim to engage as many people as possible by making the Council
        exciting, emotional — even entertaining.
      </p>
      <p>
        We will involve high profile cultural figures from across the arts, music, film &amp;
        TV both to drive public awareness and of course share their perspectives too.
      </p>

      <Scene src={following} alt="Four friends leaning in to watch something on a phone together in a café" heading="With The People" />
      <p>
        We will also create a broad media ecosystem for people to engage whoever and
        wherever they are in the country.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Social as well as legacy media to reach every generation</li>
        <li>Newsworthy viral events</li>
        <li>Live streams of Council sessions</li>
        <li>Daily highlight shows on a range of platforms</li>
        <li>
          An app where users can follow proceedings, post comments and interact through
          polls on policy ideas
        </li>
        <li>A documentary to tell the Council's story</li>
        <li>
          A portal for people to submit their own stories building an archive of our
          national memory on immigration
        </li>
      </ul>
      <Scene src={festival} alt="A crowd gathered at golden hour under festival bunting" />
      <p>
        The site itself will be accessible with music, food, exhibitions and relevant events
        to draw audiences to attend in person.
      </p>
      <p>
        The goal of it all: to show people that there is another way for our democracy to
        function, where their contributions are valued and counted, rather than ignored or
        overruled.
      </p>
      <p>The prototype on which we can build a new political system fit for whatever the future may hold.</p>

      <Scene src={child} alt="A small child standing in a long, light-filled hallway, looking up" heading="To the Future, With Hope" />
      <p>Immigration is only the start.</p>
      <p>
        We will go on to apply our Councils of the People to other issues tearing us apart,
        from cost of living to taxation to the NHS, even to our international relationships
        or the regulation of AI.
      </p>
      <p>
        While it may sound absurdly ambitious, we believe We The People speaks to a gap in
        the market – a message of hope, unity and empowerment that will strike a chord with
        millions across the country.
      </p>
      <p>If that happens, anything is possible.</p>
      <p>
        And with each step, we build a vision of what we want for our future, written by us –
        a People's Manifesto – while growing a Movement with the political force to make it
        happen.
      </p>
      <p>
        We will make this a better country. More peaceful, more united, more democratic. Fit
        for the challenges of the 21st century. A country our children will be glad to
        inherit.
      </p>
    </article>

    <!-- the doc ends on something triumphal: many of us, together -->
    <Scene
      src={celebration}
      alt="A huge crowd filling The Mall under rows of Union Jacks"
      heading="Be part of hope"
    />
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .levels__intro {
    max-width: 46ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(3rem, 10vh, 6rem) 1.5rem clamp(2.5rem, 7vh, 4rem);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-align: center;
    text-wrap: balance;
    color: rgba(246, 244, 238, 0.86);
  }

  /* --- the three levels ---------------------------------------------------- */
  .levels {
    display: flex;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--color-wtp-bramble);
  }
  .level {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    overflow: hidden;
    flex: 1 1 0;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    min-height: 58vh;
    padding: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--color-wtp-bramble);
    transition:
      flex-grow 450ms var(--ease-out),
      background-color 300ms ease;
  }
  .level:last-child {
    border-right: 0;
  }
  /* the photograph sits under a scrim, and comes up as the panel is chosen */
  .level__img {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: -1;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    opacity: 0.22;
    transition: opacity 450ms var(--ease-out);
  }
  .level__n {
    font-family: var(--font-wordmark);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.28em;
    color: var(--color-wtp-dawn);
  }
  .level__title {
    font-family: var(--font-wordmark);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.6vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 0.95;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .level__teaser {
    max-width: 26ch;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: rgba(246, 244, 238, 0.78);
  }
  .level__cta {
    margin-top: auto;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--color-wtp-dawn);
  }
  .level:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-wtp-dawn);
    outline-offset: -4px;
  }

  /* Hover widens the chosen level and brings its line in. Touch devices get
     every line up front — there is no hover to reveal it. */
  @media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
    .level__teaser {
      opacity: 0;
      translate: 0 8px;
      transition:
        opacity 300ms var(--ease-out),
        translate 300ms var(--ease-out);
    }
    .level:hover,
    .level:focus-visible {
      flex-grow: 2;
    }
    .level:hover .level__img,
    .level:focus-visible .level__img {
      opacity: 0.5;
    }
    .level:hover .level__teaser,
    .level:focus-visible .level__teaser {
      opacity: 1;
      translate: 0 0;
      transition-delay: 120ms;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .levels {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
    .level {
      min-height: auto;
      border-right: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-wtp-bramble);
    }
    .level:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .level,
    .level__teaser {
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  /* --- sections ------------------------------------------------------------ */
  .level-section {
    scroll-margin-top: 0; /* each opens on its photograph, under the header */
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--color-wtp-dawn);
  }

  /* the two-paths banner: solid green, out to the viewport edges like a
     <Scene>, its words kept in the column */
  .prose .paths-banner {
    margin: 3rem calc(50% - 50vw);
    padding: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 5.5rem) calc(50vw - 50%);
    background: var(--color-wtp-green);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.4;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* Rules of the Game — paper card, ink type, like the back of a board game */
  .game-card {
    margin: 3.4rem 0;
    padding: clamp(1.6rem, 5vw, 2.6rem);
    border-radius: 1.1rem;
    background: var(--color-wtp-paper);
    color: var(--color-wtp-ink);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px var(--color-wtp-night), 0 0 0 8px var(--color-wtp-dawn);
  }
  .game-card__head {
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
    padding-bottom: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 2px dashed rgba(0, 22, 12, 0.25);
  }
  .game-card__meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .game-card__meta span {
    padding: 0.2rem 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--color-wtp-green);
    color: var(--color-wtp-paper);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .game-card__rules {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    margin: 1.2rem 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: rule;
  }
  .game-card__rules li {
    counter-increment: rule;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.2rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .game-card__rules li::before {
    content: counter(rule);
    position: static;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-wtp-dawn);
    color: var(--color-wtp-ink);
    font-family: var(--font-wordmark);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .game-card__golden {
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
    background: rgba(22, 48, 31, 0.08);
  }
  .game-card__golden strong {
    color: var(--color-wtp-green);
  }
  .game-card__go {
    margin: 1.2rem 0 0 !important;
    font-family: var(--font-wordmark);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--color-wtp-green);
  }

  /* the plan's three stages: a small dawn label over the stage's name */
  .stage {
    margin: 2.6rem 0;
  }
  .stage__when {
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem !important;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-wtp-dawn);
  }
  .stage h3,
  .game-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    font-family: var(--font-wordmark);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.2rem);
    line-height: 1;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .game-card .stage__when {
    color: var(--color-wtp-green);
  }
  .game-card h3 {
    color: var(--color-wtp-green);
  }
</style>

<script is:inline>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-level]').forEach(function (el) {
      el.addEventListener('click', function () {
        window.posthog?.capture('be_part_level_clicked', { level: el.dataset.level });
      });
    });
  });
</script>
